From cd9721e1a9fb6ab883979e19693cae85bd06ed02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:31:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/28] console hand-off: list finished builds for a console's
 client downloads

A per-build choice (no / hidden / published, default RDGEN_PUBLISH_DEFAULT;
off and not shown while that is empty) is stored on the build, together
with the label to show and whether a preset permanent password is baked
in. When such a build succeeds, the poller touches DATA_DIR/publish.pending.

rdgen never writes into the console. A job outside rdgen runs
`manage.py rdgen_publish pending` (JSON: builds and their checked file
names, sizes and sha256), imports the files itself, then records the
result with `manage.py rdgen_publish mark <uuid> done|failed|skipped`.
The build page shows that result.

A client that carries a password (the preset permanent password, or
default-connect-password, proxy-password, preset-address-book-password
or a proxy-url with credentials in the Other boxes) cannot be sent to a
public downloads page: the form and the API refuse "published" for it,
and the pending list reports such builds as hidden.
